linux-g13-driver – Authors and Origin
=====================================

Original project
  linux-g13-driver by Jim Gupta (2011), published on Google Code
  (code.google.com/p/linux-g13-driver) under the GNU GPL v2.
  According to the original project description, parts of the driver
  code were based on ecraven/g13 (https://github.com/ecraven/g13).

Contributors (from the git history)
  Jim Gupta      – original driver and Java configuration tool (2011)
  Tetz95         – contributions (2015)
  Jason Herrlich – contributions (2021)
  Lordbooker     – modernized fork: C++ driver, Qt6 configuration tool,
                   packaging (2025–2026)

Third-party artwork
  Tux (in the LCD start animation) was originally drawn by Larry Ewing
  (lewing@isc.tamu.edu) with The GIMP. Use and modification are permitted
  provided this is acknowledged. The LCD version is a simplified 1-bit
  redraw.

All contributions are distributed under the GNU General Public License,
version 2 only (GPL-2.0-only). See the file LICENSE.
